The counterpoint is accurate.  If you are playing poorly enough to lose
300HP (with the corresponding AC that normally comes with screwing
around long enough to gain 300HP), then you are going to lose the other
300HP anyway.  Poor play can ruin any advantage.

Plus, a potion of full healing will also give you an extra 300HP, as
long as you have the sense to have it on hand so it only takes a single
turn to drink it -- and you can _make_ potions of full healing far more
easily than you can arrange to find AoLS.

